## Findings
<!-- ID: findings -->
### Finding 1: Council MCP source authority for hooks

Durable source authority:
- Registry/default hook behavior: `src/council_mcp/templates/defaults/hooks/registry.yaml:1-200`.
- Registration model and destinations: `src/council_mcp/hook_specs.py:11-76`, `:218-342`, `:345-473`.
- Runtime hook script source: `src/council_mcp/templates/claude/runtime_hooks/*.py`; repo overrides resolve first from `.council/templates/claude/runtime_hooks/<file>`, then package templates (`hook_specs.py:345-369`).
- Compiler/install pipeline: `sync_canonical_hook_source()` seeds `.council/hooks/*` while preserving local overrides unless forced (`hook_specs.py:146-195`); generation writes `.claude/hooks/*` (`compiler/phases/hooks.py:117-159`); reconciliation writes `.claude/settings.json`, prunes duplicate generated `.claude/settings.local.json` handlers, and materializes `.codex/hooks/*` (`compiler/phases/hooks.py:209-298`, `:301-444`).
- Codex config merge preserves operator-authored hook entries, prunes compiler-owned `.codex/hooks/` entries, and re-renders generated entries (`codex_toml.py:472-561`).
- `council update` is the expected operator path for source sync and materialization: `update_cmd.py:1871-1885`, `compiler/update_pipeline.py:118-164`, and `compiler/phases/generation.py:120-132`.

Generated/stale outputs:
- Existing generated hook copies in `scribe_mcp/.codex/hooks`, `scribe_mcp/.claude/hooks`, or any local generated outputs are non-authoritative for this addendum.
- Generated surfaces are acceptable proof only after source-to-output parity is checked against the Council MCP template/compiler chain.

### Finding 2: Hook paths that interact with Scribe or observe Scribe tools

| Hook/source file | Generated destination | Scribe interaction | Blocking behavior | Fallback behavior | Latency risk | Rollout risk |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `templates/claude/runtime_hooks/post_tool.py:273-315`, `:318-423` | `.claude/hooks/post_tool.py`; `.codex/hooks/post_tool.py` | Observes `mcp__scribe__set_project`; writes binding cache/session record/active binding; resolves project/workspace; logs every tool with project context | Synchronous local file writes plus possible HTTP `bind_project`, `get_binding`, `tool_log`; default HookClient timeout comes from config, default 5.0s (`hooks/client.py:104-111`) | Self-heals local cache before HTTP; catches failures; falls back to local `.claude/logs/tool_calls.jsonl` style file logging | Highest: Scribe call may finish, then hook still waits on bind/get/log HTTP calls outside Scribe timing | Broad install can make Scribe feel slow even when Scribe payload is fast; must instrument hook phases separately |
| `templates/claude/runtime_hooks/post_tool.py:201-270` | `.claude/hooks/post_tool.py`; `.codex/hooks/post_tool.py` | Observes `mcp__council-v2__open_session`; stores Council/Scribe binding data for later Scribe project context | Parses response, writes cache/state, may call HTTP `bind_session` | Self-heal writes local cache before HTTP; no-op when no Council session id | Medium: can add first-turn wait after open_session | Binding integrity risk if workspace/persona mismatch or daemon unavailable; tests cover fail-open/self-heal |
| `templates/claude/runtime_hooks/session_start.py:167-195`, `:245-375` | `.claude/hooks/session_start.py`; `.codex/hooks/session_start.py` | Injects active Scribe project, workspace, and optional recent Scribe digest; calls session/context and session/start HTTP endpoints | One short 1.5s session-context HTTP lane; then regular HookClient `session_start` call using default timeout | On session-context failure returns `None`; on session-start failure writes `.claude/logs/hook_sessions.jsonl` | Medium/high on startup: two HTTP paths can run before prompt context appears; only one has fixed 1.5s timeout | Startup context can show stale/unbound hints if binding state is wrong; privacy risk if recent digest includes sensitive progress summaries |
| `templates/claude/runtime_hooks/user_prompt_submit.py:75-193` | `.claude/hooks/user_prompt_submit.py`; `.codex/hooks/user_prompt_submit.py` | Reads binding cache/active binding and session state; injects Scribe project status into prompt context | Synchronous local file reads/writes; optional extension hook invocation | No HTTP; missing binding emits explicit unbound hint | Low/medium: repeated every prompt, but local only unless extension does work | Context correctness risk if cache/active record drift; extensions can widen behavior |
| `templates/claude/runtime_hooks/pre_tool.py:177-328` | `.claude/hooks/pre_tool.py`; `.codex/hooks/pre_tool.py` | Does not call Scribe MCP, but can govern Scribe/Council tool use via governance state and urgent blocks | Reads `.council/api_key`; targeted urgent blocks may call Council web `/api/sessions/by-pid/<pid>` with timeout=2 | Catches failures and allows when lookup fails; governance state missing means allow | Medium only when urgent targeted lookup path is active | False blocks or slow approvals can be mistaken for Scribe slowness; API key/local web availability matters |
| `templates/claude/runtime_hooks/base.py:225-360`, `:391-520`, `:850-920` | shared helper in `.claude/hooks/base.py`; `.codex/hooks/base.py` | Stores binding cache, session state, active/recent project records used by Scribe context hooks; loads HookClient and optional extensions | Local filesystem work; extension import/call can run arbitrary downstream code | Most writes fail-open with debug log; extension exceptions swallowed | Medium cumulative overhead due to per-call local writes and optional extensions | Source-authority and privacy risk if downstream `.council/hooks/extensions.py` does network/secrets work |
| `hooks/client.py:82-174`, `:176-221`, `:334-452` | imported by runtime hooks | Sends hook HTTP calls for tool log, session start/end, bind project/session, get binding, session context | Default request timeout from config (`council.hooks.request_timeout`, default 5.0s); session-context lane fixed 1.5s | Some callers catch exceptions; `get_binding` returns error dict; session-context returns `None` | High for PostToolUse because bind/get/log can each use default timeout if daemon hangs | Install gate must verify timeout config and fail-open behavior before broad rollout |
| `web/routes/hooks.py:154-202`, `:265-374`, `:433-603`, `:605-731` | Council web hook endpoints | Writes tool/session JSONL logs; binds sessions/projects; reads Scribe PROGRESS_LOG directly for recent digest | Server-side DB/session lookup for bind_session; direct file reads for recent digest | Endpoints generally return JSON errors; session/context tolerates missing digest | Medium: endpoint server work adds latency to hook HTTP calls | Privacy/secrets: hook auth uses `X-Hook-Secret`; recent digest can expose progress messages; must keep local-only/trusted assumptions explicit |

### Finding 3: Existing tests support source authority and current fallback claims

- `tests/test_hook_specs.py:15-38` proves canonical hook source seeding and local override preservation.
- `tests/test_hook_specs.py:81-124` proves packaged Codex behaviors render to command hooks under `.codex/hooks/` with documented degradations.
- `tests/test_runtime_hook_generation.py:156-214` proves Codex hooks materialize from the same package source, are idempotent, and dry-run writes nothing.
- `tests/test_runtime_hook_generation.py:258-335` proves operator Codex hook content is preserved and generated hooks are fixed-point merged into config.
- `tests/test_runtime_hooks_binding.py:134-272` proves `set_project` and `open_session` self-heal local cache on daemon failure/401/no-httpx and canonical HTTP success overwrites local cache.
- `tests/test_runtime_hooks_binding.py:1273-1322` and `:1434-1496` prove session-context HTTP lane fails open and uses the fixed 1.5s timeout.
- `tests/test_hooks/test_hook_client.py:76-144` proves hook secret resolution priority and config fallback; `:190-228` proves `log_tool` payload includes duration/project/repo fields, but PostToolUse currently calls it without a real measured duration (`post_tool.py:361-368`).


